WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 line:92%
-Thanks for being here, Jake.

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.268 size:88% position:44%
-Thanks for having me.
-And thank you, as well.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
After you saw Amanda,
you ordered a drink, as well.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want booze, too.
-All right, there you go.

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's right there.
-Thank you.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:08.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is this mine?
-There you go.

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
And cheers.
-Cheers.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you very much.
-Thank you for having me.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my God.
I'm so happy.

00:00:12.746 --> 00:00:14.848 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.883 align:start size:94% position:6%
We met briefly
when you hosted --

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were a musical guest,
excuse me, at "SNL" in 2004.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:22.322
It was a fantastic performance.
It was one of my favorite shows.

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:24.491 size:88% position:44%
Hosted by Colin Farrell.
Cameo by Lindsay Lohan.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:26.659 size:75% position:38%
-Memories. Memories.
Look at those pants.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:29.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Actually, this backless

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.264 line:92%
woman's jump suit I was wearing

00:00:31.264 --> 00:00:32.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
caused a lot of controversy
at the time.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:33.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did it, really?
-Yeah.

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:36.369
-What was the controversy?
-I got a lot of hate mail.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:39.139
-I mean, I guess 2004,
I would've thought people

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
were maybe a little more
forward-thinking.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:41.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Shoulderless,
plunging neckline.

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I don't know.
But I have good memories.

00:00:43.977 --> 00:00:46.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good memories.
And a lot happened.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:48.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
You turned 40,
you did a Broadway show,

00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
solo album, and a memoir.
-Yeah.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:52.852 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-"Boys Keep Swinging."

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why the title
"Boys Keep Swinging"?

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
-David Bowie is my,
like, number one.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.993
You know, when I was growing up,
he was just my absolute --

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:01.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
I discovered him
when I was 8 years old.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:05.632
And the album, "Lodger,"
that that song comes off of

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:06.433 line:92%
is just one of my favorites.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:10.703 size:88% position:44%
And when he passed away,
it was such a beautiful,

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.138 size:81% position:41% line:92%
sad, and special week.

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:13.139 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And I was just going --

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.442
Every night, I was going
to Bowie parties and stuff.

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:18.578
And that song came on one night,
and I was like,

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
"That's what
I'm gonna call the book."

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.347 line:92%
-It's such a fantastic song.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's so anthemic,
and you're obviously --

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:26.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had to go
and revisit a time.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:28.254 size:78% position:39%
You separate the book
into three sections.

00:01:28.254 --> 00:01:28.988 line:92%
You have Scissor Sisters,

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
you have youth,
and you have New York.

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:33.560 size:88% position:44%
You lived in New York --
When did you move here?

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:35.095 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-I moved here in 1999.

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:39.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yeah, it was a very
different time than it is now.

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:40.567 line:92%
You know, I was living in a --

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:43.002 size:75% position:38%
Basically in a place
that was like a --

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was on South 1st street
in Williamsburg,

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:47.006 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and it was like...

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
It rained and my room.
It was like this raw loft.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.812
There was basically a toilet,
like, next to the kitchen.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:53.480 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was just like --

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think you said it all
when it rained in your room.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:59.419
I think you've painted a picture
of New York real estate

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:00.587 size:81% position:41% line:92%
we can all appreciate.

00:02:00.587 --> 00:02:01.521 line:92%
-It seeped down the walls.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:04.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you --
Obviously, you are a musician,

00:02:04.124 --> 00:02:05.325 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you were also
a go-go dancer.

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was one of the ways
you made ends meet.

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.461
-Yeah.
That's how I started performing.

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:10.897 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, give it up
for go-go dancing.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:13.066 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:16.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was so much fun.
I mean, I loved the attention,

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:19.139
I loved getting up on, you know,
up in a bar

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
and taking my clothes off
and having fun.

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.809 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.809 --> 00:02:24.410 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I would just get --

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would have
the time of my life.

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, I realized, like,
"Oh, this is kind of

00:02:27.247 --> 00:02:28.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
getting boring."
Like, "What else can I do?"

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:31.584
And then, I was like, "Should
I be a singing go-go dancer?"

00:02:31.584 --> 00:02:33.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's how
I started making music.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:37.457
-It's fantastic. I will say,
and I'm not just saying this.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
We talked for weeks
about how much fun

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.896
you seemed to be having on stage
when you performed at "SNL"

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you dance
with such incredible joy.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:48.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm not surprised to hear
that that was something

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you had done
for years and years.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:52.472
-Yeah, it's being on stage
and, like, just boogying.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:56.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I love that
what I do as a job

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.243 size:81% position:41% line:92%
is, basically, like --

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
If I did what I do, like,
out in the street,

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd get arrested or something.
-Sure.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like, it's just --
It's like I get to basically

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:04.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
act like
a completely insane person.

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:06.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You --
And you've taken a lot.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:09.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've put a lot
of your costumes on stage.

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:09.956 line:92%
Not just in our "SNL" costume,

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
but here are some that
you've actually worn on stage.

00:03:12.859 --> 00:03:14.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want to tell me
some of your favorites there?

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This is my all-time favorite.
This was like a woman's

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:21.501
Vivienne Westwood pair of, like,
shorts that I found.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:25.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
That was a tablecloth
that I got from catering.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:27.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were in Scotland, and I was
gonna wear something else,

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:29.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I just pulled
that tablecloth off.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
This was a Glastonbury outfit
that was knit

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:34.247
that started falling off my body
while I was performing.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it just started
unraveling.

00:03:35.715 --> 00:03:36.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, they always say
that's the risk.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:41.955 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:45.124
You -- You know,
I assume you've had many things

00:03:45.124 --> 00:03:45.959 line:92%
that happened in your career

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
that make you want
to pinch yourself

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you can't believe
they're happening to you.

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.264 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Cher tracked you down.

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:53.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Cher tracked me down, yeah,
on a --

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.602 line:92%
-How did Cher track you down?

00:03:55.602 --> 00:03:56.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
-On Twitter.
-Okay.

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.304 size:75% position:38%
-I was having, like,
a really gnarly day,

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was flipping
through Twitter.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.974
And, you know, she writes
in all caps sometimes.

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:02.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So there was -- I just --

00:04:02.775 --> 00:04:04.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was just flipping through
the 2,000 people

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:09.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
I follow or whatever,
and just saw like all caps.

00:04:09.349 --> 00:04:11.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so you stop
when you see Cher writing.

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I'm just like,
"Oh, it's Cher."

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.988 line:92%
And then, she said, "Jake,

00:04:14.988 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been searching
for your number,

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:18.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I can't find it anywhere.
Please get ahold of me."

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:21.127
And I was like,
I wrote Twitter back, actually,

00:04:21.127 --> 00:04:23.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was like,
"Is she talking to me?"

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:24.764 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:27.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the consensus
was that she was,

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were on the phone
like two hours later,

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.003 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and then, I recorded --

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
I sang on one of her singles
the next day.

00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's incredible.
-It was a good memory.

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:36.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a good memory.
Lot of fun.

00:04:36.042 --> 00:04:36.843 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:41.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You got to --
You got to meet Elton John.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:42.982 line:92%
-Yeah, like, good friends.

00:04:42.982 --> 00:04:44.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've written
tons of stuff together.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I've --
Over the years, you know,

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:48.621 size:75% position:38%
I get to be on stage
with John sometimes

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:50.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Queens of the Stone Age.
-There you go.

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:53.059 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:53.059 --> 00:04:55.028 size:84% position:42%
-Which is -- I mean,
Queens of the Stone Age

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:55.928 line:92%
is one of my favorite, favorite,

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
favorite, favorite, favorite
bands of all time.

00:04:58.064 --> 00:05:00.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just getting
to sing with them sometimes

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.968 size:88% position:44%
and performing with them
is just like, you know,

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
just one of
the highlights of my life.

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, yeah, I get to do
all this awesome --

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:08.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's a pretty fun life
I get to lead.

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:09.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was that your takeaway?
I mean, I'm always --

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:12.378
You know, again,
because you've written a memoir.

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:14.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, you're not --
Obviously, you're only 40,

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you've lived a lot of life
in those 40 years.

00:05:16.983 --> 00:05:19.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'll say.
-When you finished this --

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
did you have a sense of that?

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
When you finished it,
were you like,

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:24.090 line:92%
"Man, I've gotten a lot done"?

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I realized
what a whore I've been.

00:05:26.626 --> 00:05:27.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.729 size:75% position:38%
-Over all the years,
because you don't --

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.397 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you really, you don't --

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:32.198 line:92%
And I mean that in the best way.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:35.568
You don't really -- I don't know
if I can say that on TV, but...

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.970 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You said it in the book,
so, yeah.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
you think you're fine,

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.040
and you think you've lived this
like, normal life,

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:42.241 size:75% position:38%
and then, you get it
all down on paper,

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:45.345
and you're like, "Wow, I've
slept with a lot of people."

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:46.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:47.880 line:92%
Even just when you do an index,

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're like,
"This is a lot of names."

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:50.149 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-A lot of thank-yous.

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:52.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a lot of thank-yous
in the back.

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:53.386 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:56.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I'm sure
they all thank you, as well.

00:05:56.189 --> 00:05:59.425
And let me follow
by thanking you for being here.

